  "Notes": "Intermediate-width low-pass:low-pass passband filter of Fig. 3\nSpecification: Passband between the reflection bands of stacks at 0.7152 lambda0 and 1.3853 lambda0.\nReported: Fig. 3 curve b: wider passband than a, roughly lambda0/lambda ~0.77-1.22, with a transmittance dip near the long-wavelength side (low lambda0/lambda) (read off plot, approximate).\nNotes: Same assumptions as McKenney1970-Fig3a. QWOT at lambda0: stack 1 layers 0.7152 (H/2 0.3576), stack 2 layers 1.3853 (H/2 0.69265), M and H' 1.0. 32 layers.\nLayers from Fig. 3 caption, p. 2437 (lambda1 = 0.7152 lambda0, lambda2 = 1.3853 lambda0); structure from Fig. 2 caption; layer 1 faces the incident medium.\nNot checked: the paper reports this design only as plots.",
